      "repair_reason": "- [P1] A maintainer must choose the public capability-CLI input-size contract before an automated repair can safely retain, remove, or document the new limits.; Needs attention: The patch improves pathname-race handling but does not actually enforce its claimed descriptor-bound resource limit against mutation of the already-open file.; Review finding: [P1] Do not impose an unapproved CLI input-size contract — src/cl... (sha=ab73995ae24331d5f045130458a5a4b9c79bf260)",
      "review_summary": "The branch replaces concurrent path-based capability-CLI media reads with sequential descriptor-bound reads and adds 100 MiB per-file plus 500 MiB aggregate input budgets.\n\nPR surface: Source +42. Total +42 across 1 file.\n\nReproducibility: yes. from source: after `handle.stat()` validates a small file, another writer can extend that same open inode before `handle.readFile()` consumes it, which can exceed the validated budget. The compatibility effect is also directly reproducible by passing a currently accepted media file above either newly introduced limit.",
